  "body": "Rung 1 of the app/UI-on-wasm work. **This is a partial PR**: the domain layer builds and links for wasm32. The UI does not yet.\n\n## What builds\n- `web/build-app-wasm.sh` builds `camcraft-app` for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` and links `camcraft-cli.wasm`. That covers flecs' C, boa, truck, clipper2 and rayon. Before this, only geometry, cl and post compiled for wasm32.\n- flecs' C needs a libc, and this target has none. The script downloads the wasi-sysroot 34 tarball, checks its sha256, and passes its headers through `CFLAGS_wasm32_unknown_unknown`. It also adds `-D__COSMOCC__` (flecs' generic-POSIX path) and `-D__wasi__`. At link time its `libc.a` resolves malloc, printf, pthread, clock and the rest.\n- flecs_ecs 0.2.2 and flecs_ecs_sys 0.2.1 do not compile for wasm32 as published; upstream says that support is still in progress. The script copies both crates and makes three edits to the copies:\n  - `libc::FILE` becomes `c_void`.\n  - The pre-generated bindings use `\"C\"` in place of `\"C-unwind\"`.\n  - meta_fn_types' wasm-gated `WorldRef`/`Entity` import is no longer gated.\n\n  The copies are used through `cargo --config patch.crates-io...` for this build only. Each edit checks that its patch point is still there, so a flecs bump that moves one fails the build instead of passing silently. The tracked `Cargo.lock` is restored when the script exits.\n- The `wasm` job in `ci.yml` now runs the script. Like every job in that file it is `workflow_dispatch` only, so it adds no push, PR or schedule trigger.\n- No Rust source, manifest or lock file changed, so the native build is unchanged.\n\n## Readings\n- Local run (Windows, Git Bash, clang 21.1.8): `web/build-app-wasm.sh` finished in 2m52s and printed `linked .../wasm32-unknown-unknown/debug/camcraft-cli.wasm` (270 MB, debug). Afterwards `git status` was clean, which shows the lock was restored.\n- The linked module has two groups of imports:\n  - the wasm-bindgen placeholders;\n  - nine `wasi_snapshot_preview1` functions: `clock_time_get`, `fd_close`, `fd_fdstat_get`, `fd_prestat_get`, `fd_prestat_dir_name`, `fd_seek`, `fd_write`, `poll_oneoff`, `proc_exit`.\n- I have not run the CI job. It is manual and the Actions budget applies.\n\n## What does not build yet, and why (#31 stays open)\n`cargo build -p camcraft-ui --lib --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`, with the flecs patches applied, stops at:\n```\nerror[E0407]: method `bytes` is not a member of trait `egui::DroppedFile`\n  --> egui-winit-0.36.2\\src\\dropped_file.rs:19:5\nerror[E0046]: not all trait items implemented, missing: `bytes_async`\nerror: could not compile `egui-winit` (lib) due to 2 previous errors\n```\negui-winit 0.36.2 is native-only, so the browser shell needs eframe's web runner in its place. After that, the following are still owed; details are in `docs/decisions/31-wasm-ui.md`:\n- Move `shell_layout` out of `shell.rs` so both shells call it.\n- Bring up the GPU asynchronously. About ten `pollster::block_on` sites remain.\n- Replace the synchronous `rfd::FileDialog` (9 sites) with an async version or an `<input type=file>` seam.\n- Add a `web_time` seam for `std::time::Instant`, which panics on this target.\n- Run work inline where the code calls `std::thread::spawn`.\n- Write a JS shim for the nine wasi imports.\n- Pin wasm-bindgen CLI 0.2.129.\n\n## Tests\nNo Rust code changed, so there are no new pinning tests. The proof is the script itself, run locally above. `bash -n web/build-app-wasm.sh` passes.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/31-wasm-ui.md`.\n\nChangelog: none (build tooling only; there is no user-visible change until the UI rung lands)\n\nRefs #31\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
